  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multi-profile with scvi_n200 is the clear best so far (0.653 with transformer, 0.650 with avgpool), and image-only ResNet50 is very weak (0.208). The dominant open question is whether adding an image modality to the best RNA configuration can push accuracy above 0.653. This experiment (config_039) extends the best RNA setup (scvi_n200, multi-profile, transformer) by adding the strongest available image encoder (ViT-L, untested) with weighted fusion, which allows the model to adaptively down-weight the image signal if it is uninformative. This isolates the effect of modality addition while holding all RNA-side choices at their empirically best values. It is the best use of experiment 7 because it directly tests the single most impactful remaining design question (does multimodal help?) before the budget runs out, and the result will determine whether the final 2 experiments should refine a multimodal config or confirm RNA-only as optimal."
}

